title: "Combobox"
description: "A button that opens a searchable list to pick one option, built from the popover and command components."
---

<script lang="ts">
	import Demo from "./demo.svelte";
</script>

# Combobox

Picks one option from a list that is too long to scan, by typing to filter it. The trigger is an outline `Button` that opens a `Popover`, and the popover holds a `Command` with a search input. Selecting an item sets the value, closes the popover, and returns focus to the trigger.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Combobox, ComboboxTrigger, ComboboxValue, ComboboxContent, ComboboxInput, ComboboxList, ComboboxEmpty, ComboboxGroup, ComboboxItem } from "#lib/components/ui/combobox/index.js";

	const frameworks = [
		{ value: "sveltekit", label: "SvelteKit" },
		{ value: "next", label: "Next.js" },
		{ value: "nuxt", label: "Nuxt" },
	];
</script>

<Combobox>
	<ComboboxTrigger class="trigger">
		<ComboboxValue placeholder="Select framework..." />
	</ComboboxTrigger>
	<ComboboxContent>
		<ComboboxInput placeholder="Search framework..." />
		<ComboboxList>
			<ComboboxEmpty>No framework found.</ComboboxEmpty>
			<ComboboxGroup>
				{#each frameworks as framework (framework.value)}
					<ComboboxItem value={framework.value}>{framework.label}</ComboboxItem>
				{/each}
			</ComboboxGroup>
		</ComboboxList>
	</ComboboxContent>
</Combobox>

<style>
	:global(.trigger) {
		width: 12.5rem;
	}
</style>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/combobox.json
```

## Anatomy

`Combobox` holds the value and renders a `Popover`. `ComboboxTrigger` renders the outline button with a chevron, and `ComboboxValue` inside it shows the selected item's text or the placeholder. Give the trigger a fixed width with a `class`, so it does not resize as the value changes.

`ComboboxContent` opens a popover as wide as the trigger, with at least `12.5rem`, and holds a `Command` that starts on the selected item. `ComboboxItem` selects its `value` and shows a check mark while selected. `ComboboxInput`, `ComboboxList`, `ComboboxEmpty`, `ComboboxGroup`, and `ComboboxSeparator` are the `Command` parts, so they filter and navigate the same way.

## Groups

Use `ComboboxGroup` with a `heading` and `ComboboxSeparator` to organize long lists. Groups hide while none of their items match. Add `keywords` to an item to match words that are not shown, such as a timezone abbreviation.

<Demo section="groups" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<ComboboxList>
	<ComboboxEmpty>No timezone found.</ComboboxEmpty>
	<ComboboxGroup heading="Americas">
		<ComboboxItem value="America/New_York" keywords={["est", "eastern"]}>New York</ComboboxItem>
		<ComboboxItem value="America/Los_Angeles" keywords={["pst", "pacific"]}>Los Angeles</ComboboxItem>
	</ComboboxGroup>
	<ComboboxSeparator />
	<ComboboxGroup heading="Europe">
		<ComboboxItem value="Europe/London" keywords={["gmt"]}>London</ComboboxItem>
	</ComboboxGroup>
</ComboboxList>
```

## Trigger

`ComboboxTrigger` renders an outline button with a chevron. To open the popover from any other element, pass a `trigger` snippet and put the `ComboboxValue` inside it. It receives the popover trigger's `props`, with the ARIA attributes, the handlers, and the attachment that places the popover, plus `disabled`. Spread them onto the element.

<Demo section="trigger" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<ComboboxTrigger>
	{#snippet trigger({ props })}
		<Button variant="ghost" {...props}>
			<ComboboxValue placeholder="Select framework..." />
			<ChevronsUpDownIcon />
		</Button>
	{/snippet}
</ComboboxTrigger>
```

## Controlled

Use `bind:value` to read and set the selected value, or `onValueChange` to run code on each selection. Use `bind:open` or `onOpenChange` for the popover. Without either, set `defaultValue` to start with a selection.

Items register their text when the list first opens, so `ComboboxValue` shows a starting value's raw `value` until then. Pass `label` to show the right text from the start.

<Demo section="controlled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	let framework = $state("sveltekit");
	const frameworkLabel = $derived(frameworks.find((item) => item.value === framework)?.label);
</script>

<Combobox bind:value={framework}>
	<ComboboxTrigger class="trigger">
		<ComboboxValue placeholder="Select framework..." label={frameworkLabel} />
	</ComboboxTrigger>
	<ComboboxContent>...</ComboboxContent>
</Combobox>
<p>Value: {framework || "none"}</p>
```

## Forms

Set `name` to submit the value with a form through a hidden input.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<form method="POST">
	<Combobox name="framework">...</Combobox>
</form>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` on `Combobox` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg` to change the trigger, the input, and the items together. The default is `md`, and the corner radius follows the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Combobox size="lg">...</Combobox>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` on `Combobox` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius of the trigger, popover, and items.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Combobox rounded="3xl">...</Combobox>
```

## States

Set `disabled` on `Combobox` to dim the trigger and block opening, or on `ComboboxItem` to block one option. The arrow keys skip disabled items.

<Demo section="states" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Combobox disabled>...</Combobox>
<ComboboxItem value="remix" disabled>Remix</ComboboxItem>
```

## Overrides

`ComboboxTrigger` takes its own `variant`, `size`, and `rounded`, and `ComboboxContent` takes `size` and `rounded`. Each wins over the combobox's for that part only. `ComboboxItem` takes `rounded` to set that item's exact radius.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Combobox>
	<ComboboxTrigger variant="ghost" size="sm">
		<ComboboxValue placeholder="Pick a framework" />
	</ComboboxTrigger>
	<ComboboxContent size="lg">
		<ComboboxItem value="svelte" rounded="pill">Svelte</ComboboxItem>
	</ComboboxContent>
</Combobox>
```

## API

`ComboboxTrigger` passes extra attributes to its `Button` and ignores them when a `trigger` snippet is given, `ComboboxValue` extends `span`, and `ComboboxContent` and `ComboboxItem` extend `div`. See the `Command` docs for the props of the shared parts. Selected items set `data-checked` for custom styles.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface ComboboxOptions {
	/** Value of the selected item; supports `bind:value` */
	value?: string;
	/** Starting value when `value` is not set */
	defaultValue?: string;
	/** Called with the new value when an item is selected */
	onValueChange?: (value: string) => void;
	/** Whether the popover is shown; supports `bind:open` */
	open?: boolean;
	/** Called when the popover opens or closes */
	onOpenChange?: (open: boolean) => void;
	/** Dims the trigger and blocks opening */
	disabled?: boolean;
	/** Form field name; the value submits through a hidden input */
	name?: string;
	/** Trigger height, input height, and item size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of the trigger, popover, and items; follows `size` when omitted. `pill` makes the panels pills too, which can clip their items, so use `3xl` or `4xl` for round panels */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

interface TriggerProps extends Omit<CompProps<"button">, "children"> {
	/** Content of the default trigger button, such as a `ComboboxValue` */
	children?: Snippet;
	/** Custom trigger; spread `props` onto the element that opens the popover */
	trigger?: Snippet<[{ props: TriggerAttrs }]>;
	/** Style of the default trigger button; defaults to `outline` */
	variant?: ButtonProps["variant"];
	/** Size of the default trigger button; overrides the combobox's `size` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of the default trigger button; overrides the combobox's `rounded` */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

interface ValueProps extends CompProps<"span"> {
	/** Text shown when no item is selected */
	placeholder?: string;
	/** Text for the selected value; needed for a starting value before the list has opened once */
	label?: string;
}

interface ItemProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Value set on the combobox when this item is chosen */
	value: string;
	/** Text shown in `ComboboxValue`; defaults to the item's text */
	label?: string;
	/** Extra words that also match the item, such as synonyms */
	keywords?: string[];
	/** Blocks selecting the item; the arrow keys skip it */
	disabled?: boolean;
	/** Corner radius of this item with this exact value; overrides the list's item radius */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

interface ContentProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Item size of this popover; overrides the combobox's `size` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius of this popover, with items one step smaller; overrides the combobox's `rounded`. `pill` makes it a pill too, which can clip its items, so use `3xl` or `4xl` to stay round */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}
```
